    "truncatedDescription": "Try out Joplin, one of the best Open Source Note taking apps: https://joplinapp.org/?source=TheLinuxEXP\r\n\r\nUse code LINUXEXPERIMENT for 25% off your first billing cycle for Joplin Cloud\r\n\r\nGrab a brand new laptop or desktop running Linux: https://...",
    "description": "Try out Joplin, one of the best Open Source Note taking apps: https://joplinapp.org/?source=TheLinuxEXP\r\n\r\nUse code LINUXEXPERIMENT for 25% off your first billing cycle for Joplin Cloud\r\n\r\nGrab a brand new laptop or desktop running Linux: https://www.tuxedocomputers.com/en#\r\n\r\n\r\n👏 SUPPORT THE CHANNEL:\r\nGet access to:\r\n- a Daily Linux News show\r\n- a weekly patroncast for more thoughts\r\n- your name in the credits\r\n\r\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@thelinuxexp/join\r\nPatreon: https://www.patreon.com/thelinuxexperiment\r\n\r\nOr, you can donate whatever you want:\r\nhttps://paypal.me/thelinuxexp\r\nLiberapay: https://liberapay.com/TheLinuxExperiment/\r\n\r\n👕 GET TLE MERCH\r\nSupport the channel AND get cool new gear: https://the-linux-experiment.creator-spring.com/\r\n\r\n#linuxnews #linuxdesktop #linux \r\n\r\nTimestamps\r\n00:00 Intro\r\n00:55 Sponsor: Joplin \r\n02:24 Netherlands goes with NixOS\r\n05:38 Android is less and less open source\r\n08:09 GoogleBook OS introduced as a Linux based system\r\n10:57 KDE's proposed AI policy leads to massive backlash\r\n13:57 GNOME dev offers a \"no AI at all\" policy\r\n16:08 KDE announces their 3 mains goals for 2027\r\n18:04 SteamOS update brings many performance improvements\r\n19:51 Linux kernel 7.4 should open files 39% faster\r\n20:54 Ubuntu improves how the system behaves when out of memory\r\n22:52 Valve introduces new low latency codec for game streaming\r\n24:09 Ubuntu will update the kernel on a weekly basis\r\n25:35 Cosmic 1.9 brings two new applications\r\n27:41 reactOS now has a solid DirectX implementation\r\n29:24 Sponsor: Tuxedo Computers\r\n\r\nLinks:\r\n\r\nNetherlands goes with NixOS\r\nhttps://itsfoss.com/news/netherlands-dawo-initiative/\r\n\r\nAndroid is less and less open source\r\nhttps://itsfoss.com/news/grapheneos-android-17-qpr1-fiasco/\r\n\r\nGoogleBook OS introduced as a Linux based system\r\nhttps://www.techradar.com/computing/laptops/rethinking-the-laptop-is-a-big-undertaking-why-googlebooks-are-so-much-more-than-overpriced-chromebooks-and-apple-should-be-worried\r\n\r\nKDE's proposed AI policy leads to massive backlash\r\nhttps://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/kde-developers-attempts-at-creating-llm-guidelines-are-not-going-well/\r\nhttps://pointieststick.com/2026/09/23/kde-and-ai-and-you-and-me/\r\n\r\nGNOME dev offers a \"no AI at all\" policy\r\nhttps://blogs.gnome.org/alatiera/2026/09/23/the-gnome-llm-policy-that-i-want/\r\n\r\nKDE announces their 3 mains goals for 2027\r\nhttps://www.phoronix.com/news/KDE-Goals-To-2028\r\n\r\nSteamOS update brings many performance improvements\r\nhttps://www.gamingonlinux.com/2026/09/steamos-3-8-28-stable-released-with-big-improvements-for-steam-deck-steam-machine-and-more-hardware-support/\r\n\r\nLinux kernel 7.4 should open files 39% faster\r\nhttps://www.phoronix.com/news/Linux-7.4-Faster-Do-Open \r\n\r\nUbuntu improves how the system behaves when out of memory\r\nhttps://discourse.ubuntu.com/t/improving-ubuntu-desktop-stability-under-memory-pressure/87945\r\n\r\nValve introduces new low latency codec for game streaming\r\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/groups/homestream/discussions/0/564794422009744473?snr=2\r\n\r\nUbuntu will update the kernel on a weekly basis\r\nhttps://canonical.com/blog/accelerating-delivery-of-cve-fixes-with-a-new-kernel-release-strategy\r\n\r\nCosmic 1.9 brings two new applications\r\nhttps://linuxiac.com/cosmic-desktop-1-9-adds-cosmic-viewer-on-screen-keyboard/\r\n\r\nreactOS now has a solid DirectX implementation\r\nhttps://github.com/reactos/reactos/pull/9352",
